# Browsers the storefront and admin UI must render identically on.
# Drives autoprefixer (via .postcssrc.json) for every stylesheet — global SCSS
# and inline component styles: blocks alike.
#
# Kept to browsers with native color-mix() support (Chrome/Edge 111+, Firefox
# 113+, Safari 16.4+, ~April 2023 onward). Tailwind v4's Lightning CSS engine
# reads this file too: targeting anything older (e.g. iOS 15) makes it
# "downlevel" color-mix() by REPLACING the declaration with a lossy static
# approximation for every browser, not just old ones — verified by inspecting
# compiled output, an 8% accent tint became a solid 100% accent fill. Manual
# fallback-first declarations (plain color declared before color-mix()) handle
# genuinely older browsers via the CSS cascade instead — no build-tool help
# needed, and no risk of silently degrading modern rendering.
